00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:06,600
 So here, the molar would be experiencing a mesial force and an extrusive force that much

94
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,160
 is the same.

95
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:13,840
 Both cases for the canine, they're going to be experiencing distal force and an extrusive

96
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,440
 force.

97
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:19,600
 What changes is which arch is being affected.

98
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:27,320
 So inter-archalastics will always apply an extrusive force, but the mesial first distal

